# beta, attempt 2. Attempt 1 (s1opt_FAILED_dark_state.out) followed cistarget 1
# by INDEX and lost the bright state at cycle 12: root 1 went from f = 1.559
# (93->94) to f = 0.0001 while the bright 93->95 state moved to root 3. It then
# spent 130 cycles relaxing onto a DARK state. That is not a tracking slip alone
# -- a gas-phase GFP chromophore genuinely relaxes on S1 by twisting toward a
# dark TICT state, which the protein prevents (MD inter-ring twist is only
# 7.2 +/- 3.1 deg).
#
# Fix, both parts:
#   (a) freeze the two bridge dihedrals at their planar ground-state values, so
#       the chromophore relaxes IN PLANE as it does in the protein and the dark
#       twisted state never comes down;
#   (b) target root 3, which is the bright 93->95 state once the dark state is
#       out of the way -- verified against the character each cycle afterwards.
coordinates s0_geom.xyz
run minimize
cis yes
cisnumstates 5
cistarget 3
cismaxiter 300
method camb3lyp
basis 6-31gs
charge -1
spinmult 1
scf diis+a
threall 1.0e-13
new_minimizer yes
nstep 120
gpus 1
$constraint_freeze
dihedral 16_15_14_5
dihedral 15_14_5_4
$end
end
